# Git trunk hygiene

`master` is the only durable branch. Agent branches and worktrees are scratch.

- Create a branch only when asked. Name it `wip/<task>`.
- Never push `stash`, `local-sync`, or `safety` snapshot branches.
- Never use `git stash` as the way to save work. Commit on the task branch or leave the working tree.
- A worktree is one disposable checkout for one task. Do not start a second worktree unless the user asked for parallel work.
- When finished: land the work on `master` (fast-forward or PR), then delete the branch and remove the worktree. Do not leave a second long-lived branch.
- Before starting and before stopping, run:
  `git fetch --prune && git status && git worktree list && git branch -vv`
- Close `[gone]` remotes and leftover worktrees the same day.

```text
❌ git push origin stash-0-local-sync-2026-08-20
❌ leave 4 worktrees each holding part of the same change
✅ commit on wip/v8-affinity, merge to master, delete the branch and worktree
```
